# Trivy findings accepted for the image gate (platform LLD §12; testing.md §2; C38).
# Format, enforced by scripts/ci/images.sh (one finding per line):
#   <CVE-or-GHSA-id> # reason: <why it is acceptable>; owner: <github handle>; exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# Every entry is also recorded in SECURITY_DEPENDENCIES.md. Trivy stops honouring an entry after
# its exp: date, and the policy check fails on it, so an acceptance is always re-reviewed.
# Accepted 2026-11-10 (S9): Debian base-image packages with no fixed version (status affected,
# fix_deferred or will_not_fix); the fixable findings are removed in the Dockerfiles instead.
CVE-2023-45853 # reason: no Debian 12 fix: node statically links its own zlib, so the web server never loads system zlib1g (fixed in Debian 13: move the web image to a trixie base); owner: @Positron00; exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2025-69720 # reason: no Debian fix yet: terminal library of the base image, unused by a non-interactive server; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
CVE-2026-119373 # reason: no Debian 13 fix yet: the services never import sqlite3 and use neither FTS5 nor session changesets; owner: @Positron00; exp:2027-01-10
